# func/text/tx_mid (id 316): MID core (also LEFT and RIGHT through their wrappers).
# A = text or error, B = start (number or error), C = count (number or error). Start and count are
# truncated (clamped to +-2^23 first). Errors: A, else B, else C; start < 1 or count < 0 -> #VALUE!.
# Result A = (2, new handle) of units start .. start + count - 1 (fewer if the text is shorter).
# PC 0: errors -> return; else read [hA]. PC 1: x0 = L; n = min(count, max(0, L - s0)), s0 = start - 1;
# i0 = floor(min(s0, L) / 3), o = min(s0, L) mod 3; write [HT] = n; P0 = hA + 2 + i0, P1 = HT + 2,
# OH (T2) = HT, N1 = n, o (T3). PC 2: N1 <= 0 -> A = (2, OH), HT = P1, return; else read [P0], P0 += 1,
# F (T4) = 1. PC 3: if F: T1 = x0; F = 0; read [P0], P0 += 1. PC 4: write [P1] = word from (T1, x0) at
# offset o, masked to min(N1, 3) units; T1 = x0; P1 += 1; N1 -= 3; next PC 3 if N1 >= 4 else PC 2.
# Note: weights/func/text/tx_mid.md
